  1	//! Single authority for paying life as a cost.
  2	//!
  3	//! All cost paths that deduct life — spell additional costs (Flashback life,
  4	//! generic "Pay N life" additional costs), activated-ability costs (Greed,
  5	//! Necropotence, Phyrexian Tower family), mana-ability costs, `Effect::PayCost`
  6	//! resolution, and `UnlessCost::PayLife` — route through [`pay_life_as_cost`].
  7	//!
  8	//! Pre-validation sites (`can_activate_ability_now`, Defiler offer, legal-action
  9	//! generation) consult [`can_pay_life_cost`] so the UI never offers a cost the
 10	//! player cannot actually pay.
 11	//!
 12	//! # Rules
 13	//!
 14	//! - **CR 118.3** — A player can't pay a cost without the resources to pay it fully.
 15	//! - **CR 118.3b** — Paying life subtracts the amount from the player's life total.
 16	//!   Players can always pay 0 life.
 17	//! - **CR 119.4** — "If a player pays life, the payment is subtracted from their
 18	//!   life total; in other words, the player loses that much life." Paying life IS
 19	//!   losing life, so the deduction routes through
 20	//!   [`effects::life::apply_life_loss`] which runs the replacement pipeline.
 21	//! - **CR 119.4b** — Players can always pay 0 life, even under a pay-life prohibition.
 22	//! - **CR 119.8** — "A cost that involves having that player pay life can't be paid."
 23	
 24	use crate::game::effects::life::{apply_life_loss, ReplacementDeferred};
 25	use crate::game::static_abilities::{player_cant_pay_life_as_cost, player_has_cant_lose_life};
